#
# holt — Prolog for a ctags that does not have it.
#
# Loaded ONLY after holt has MEASURED that this toolchain cannot extract Prolog symbols, and
# defined under a PRIVATE name. Both matter, and the reason is not hypothetical: this definition
# used to live in the always-loaded pack under the real name `Prolog`, and the moment upstream
# ctags gained its own Prolog parser the load became FATAL — "Language \"Prolog\" already
# defined", ctags exits, and holt gets ZERO symbols from EVERY file in the repository. Silence,
# which reads as "these agents share nothing".
#
# A private name cannot collide with a builtin. The measurement gate means a real builtin parser
# is never replaced by these regexes when one exists.
#
### Prolog #####################################################################
--langdef=HoltProlog
--map-HoltProlog=+.pl
--map-HoltProlog=+.pro
--map-HoltProlog=+.plt
--kinddef-HoltProlog=p,predicate,predicates
--regex-HoltProlog=/^([a-z][a-zA-Z0-9_]*)[ \t]*\(/\1/p/
--regex-HoltProlog=/^:-[ \t]*(dynamic|discontiguous)[ \t]+([a-z][a-zA-Z0-9_]*)/\2/p/
